#question(title: [Doughnut])[
  #set text(size: 13pt)

  Let $R$ be the region inside the curve with
  equation
  $
    (x - 1)^2 + y^2 = 1 .
  $
  Rotate $R$ around the line with equation
  $display(x = 4)$. The resulting solid is
  called a #emph[torus].

  + Draw a picture and convince yourself that
    a torus looks like a doughnut.
  + Set up the volume of the torus as an
    integral using $x$ as the variable
    (“cylindrical shell method"). You do not
    need to compute the integral.
  + Set up the volume of the torus as an
    integral using $y$ as the variable
    (“carrot method"). You do not need to
    compute the integral.
]
